Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "BLOCK_NUMBER": block height of the transfer – put in final SELECT and to order / group  
• "ADDRESS": contract address that emitted the event – filter to USDT contract (`'0xa614f803b6fd780986a42c78ec9c7f77e6ded13c'`)  
• "EVENT_SIGNATURE": lets us keep only ‟Transfer(address,address,uint256)” events  
• "ARGS": JSON array that contains [from, to, value] – needs `PARSE_JSON` then array subscripts `[0]`, `[1]`, `[2]`  
• "BLOCK_TIMESTAMP": optional, could be shown or used for extra filters  
• "TOPICS": alternate place to see indexed addresses, not needed once we rely on ARGS  
• "TRANSACTION_HASH" / "LOG_INDEX": can be shown for provenance if desired  

Typical conditions  
• "ADDRESS" = '0xa614f803b6fd780986a42c78ec9c7f77e6ded13c'  
• "EVENT_SIGNATURE" = 'Transfer(address,address,uint256)'        -- or its hash  
• ORDER BY (PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[2]::NUMBER / 1e6) DESC              -- biggest transfers first  
• LIMIT 3 (or LIMIT 20 for exploration queries)                    -- keep result set small  

Below are ten exploratory → final Snowflake SQL snippets (all limited to 20 rows) demonstrating how one might work toward the requested result.  
Every identifier is enclosed in double‑quotes and fully‑qualified.

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at 20 random decoded events just to understand the column layout.
SELECT *
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Show distinct event signatures that come from the USDT contract.
SELECT DISTINCT "EVENT_SIGNATURE"
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "ADDRESS" = '0xa614f803b6fd780986a42c78ec9c7f77e6ded13c'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Pull 20 rows of USDT Transfer events with raw ARGS for inspection.
SELECT "BLOCK_NUMBER",
       "ARGS",
       "TOPICS"
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "ADDRESS"         = '0xa614f803b6fd780986a42c78ec9c7f77e6ded13c'
  AND "EVENT_SIGNATURE" = 'Transfer(address,address,uint256)'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Extract the `from`, `to`, and `value` fields from ARGS as VARIANT.
SELECT PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[0]          AS "from_raw",
       PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[1]          AS "to_raw",
       PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[2]          AS "value_raw"
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "ADDRESS"         = '0xa614f803b6fd780986a42c78ec9c7f77e6ded13c'
  AND "EVENT_SIGNATURE" = 'Transfer(address,address,uint256)'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Convert the numeric value into whole‑token USDT (divide by 1,000,000).
SELECT PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[2]::NUMBER           AS "raw_value",
       (PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[2]::NUMBER / 1e6)   AS "usdt_amount"
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "ADDRESS"         = '0xa614f803b6fd780986a42c78ec9c7f77e6ded13c'
  AND "EVENT_SIGNATURE" = 'Transfer(address,address,uint256)'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Add block number and order by the biggest transfers (still raw hex addresses).
SELECT "BLOCK_NUMBER",
       PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[0] AS "from_hex",
       PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[1] AS "to_hex",
       (PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[2]::NUMBER / 1e6) AS "usdt_amount"
FROM "GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN"."GOOG_BLOCKCHAIN_ARBITRUM_ONE_US"."DECODED_EVENTS"
WHERE "ADDRESS"         = '0xa614f803b6fd780986a42c78ec9c7f77e6ded13c'
  AND "EVENT_SIGNATURE" = 'Transfer(address,address,uint256)'
ORDER BY "usdt_amount" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Demonstrate converting destination address to TronLink/Base58 using a
--              user‑defined JavaScript function `HEX_TO_TRON` (placeholder name).
SELECT "BLOCK_NUMBER",
       PARSE_JSON("ARGS")[0]                       AS "from_hex",
